{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UcFsmbnLF4gmEetgtgPsJu","type":"tool_result","content":"module github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n\ngo 1.27\n\nrequire (\nagent\nagentjob\nbotcheck\nbudget\ncli\ncloseout\ncommitter\nconfig\nconfigcmd\nconfigsrc\ncontroller\ncostblock\ncosts\ndigest\ndocscheck\neffects\nexecutor\ngithub\ngitref\ngitx\ninitcmd\nintake\njanitor\nlabels\nlimits\nmerger\nmodelauth\npool\nprgate\nprwatch\nreaper\nredact\nrepopath\nreviewer\nreviewfix\nroles\nscanner\nservecmd\nstate\ntriage\nversioncheck\nworker\nwtlock\nls: internal/tarball: No such file or directory\nc5d12ce feat: Conflict rounds, part A: merger request path and reason-aw… (#354)\ncc5d3c8 ard(triage:engineer): #307 No plan was written. The docs would have to describe a release workflow… [skip ci]\n34ab395 ard(triage:lead): #313 This is a refactor with no behaviour change. It moves the filesystem ha… [skip ci]\n3632770 Kubernetes executor, part 1: decision record and proposal update… (#353)\na78e7e0 ard(triage:engineer): #293 Adds a repo-context section to each of the 11 embedded starter prompts… [skip ci]\nea9db63 ard(triage:engineer): #302 Plans a startup GitHub connectivity check, live-run support for a perso… [skip ci]\n0eaa949 ard(triage:lead): #307 This is a docs-only change. It adds a Homebrew install section to the R… [skip ci]\n5b7d0ba ard(triage:lead): #293 This change edits the starter role prompts embedded in internal/roles s… [skip ci]\ndocs/proposal.md:305:Kubernetes-executor details (decided, design revision 3 of [#54](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54), recorded in [#312](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/312); the work is split across later parts of #54, and #317 splits into the API layer and the executor). There is no job API on `ard serve`. **Pod shape.** `pre` fetches with the token passed through `http.extraheader` from the environment, never argv or `.git/config`; the git dir is on a `ctl` volume the agent does not mount; the role dir comes from `cfg.SHA`, so the k8s executor refuses a config without a SHA; sidecars are at pinned SHAs; the untrusted inputs and the scrub list travel in the per-job Secret, capped at 768 KiB (over the cap is a permanent failure with a named cause); `pre` copies the static `ard` binary. The `agent` container mounts only `work` and `out` and holds only its model credential via `secretKeyRef`: no GitHub token, no key, no Secret volume, no SA token. It tees stdout to `out/stdout`, enforces its own deadline, writes a done marker and reaps orphans as PID 1. `post` has its own pinned image and never runs a binary from a shared volume. It serves one route, `GET /v1/result`, on the pod IP, guarded by a preshared 32-byte `crypto/rand` key unique to the pod, mounted only in `post` and kept in memory by the controller, compared in constant time. It answers 409 until the agent has terminated and the marker exists, builds the tar in Go and never runs git, serves one request at a time, has header and idle timeouts, never logs Authorization, and exits 0 after the controller confirms or at the deadline. The transport is plain HTTP inside the cluster (the owner's choice): the key grants only this job's result, and a NetworkPolicy limits who can connect.\ndocs/proposal.md:589:- [x] **Kubernetes executor ([#54](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54)).** Decided 2026-11-24, design revision 3 ([design comment](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/54#issuecomment-7131825898), recorded in [#312](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/312)): no job API on `ard serve`; the controller pulls the result from a `post` container with a per-pod key; plain HTTP inside the cluster; stdout from a tee file, with forgeable usage figures accepted as a risk; a public `ard-agent` image; cluster settings are flags, not config; `flock` on a `ReadWriteOncePod` volume; size defaults as in Kubernetes-executor details; trufflehog off under k8s. See Kubernetes-executor